1
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,239
I was taking my kid upstairs,

2
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,280
when he rushed over

3
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:42,680
and held a knife to me.

4
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,000
Did you know him before?

5
00:01:50,799 --> 00:01:51,760
Never seen him before.

6
00:01:59,159 --> 00:01:59,599
All right.

7
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:02,079
Get some rest.

8
00:02:02,799 --> 00:02:05,000
We'll contact you if we need anything else.

9
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,560
Check with the Police Station

10
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:13,479
about her ID card application.

11
00:02:13,759 --> 00:02:14,199
Understood.

12
00:02:14,199 --> 00:02:14,599
Got it.

13
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:15,719
How is it?

14
00:02:17,199 --> 00:02:18,319
What's the situation inside?

15
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:19,680
Thank you for saving us.

16
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,080
You're welcome.

17
00:02:29,879 --> 00:02:31,319
Hope we didn't scare you just now.

18
00:02:36,639 --> 00:02:37,599
Sorry about that.

19
00:02:38,319 --> 00:02:40,199
He's had a heart condition since birth.

20
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,400
He doesn't talk much.

21
00:02:41,439 --> 00:02:42,240
He's shy with strangers.

22
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:44,840
He has a heart condition.

23
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,039
Dilated Cardiomyopathy.

24
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:48,840
Naonao.

25
00:02:52,039 --> 00:02:53,879
Naonao rarely gets this close to people.

26
00:02:55,919 --> 00:02:57,280
I guess this is him getting close to me.

27
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:00,680
He's too scared to even speak.

28
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,639
Naonao.

29
00:03:03,639 --> 00:03:04,840
Come on, make some noise!

30
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:11,639
All right.

31
00:03:12,719 --> 00:03:13,960
As long as you're okay.

32
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,560
We just came to check on you.

33
00:03:17,919 --> 00:03:18,759
We'll be heading out now.

34
00:03:19,439 --> 00:03:19,919
Let's go.

35
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:20,520
Let's go.

36
00:03:21,039 --> 00:03:21,840
Naonao?

37
00:03:25,319 --> 00:03:26,240
He's not letting us go.

38
00:03:27,759 --> 00:03:28,520
Where do you live?

39
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:31,159
Cloud Creek Road.

40
00:03:31,879 --> 00:03:34,039
Chief Liao, it's near the Special Police Unit.

41
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:34,800
Let's give them a ride back.

42
00:03:35,159 --> 00:03:35,479
Sure.

43
00:03:35,479 --> 00:03:36,280
No need, it's too much trouble.

44
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,919
It's no trouble. It's on the way.

45
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:39,719
We're giving them a ride.

46
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:40,439
Alright! Thanks for the trouble.

47
00:03:40,439 --> 00:03:41,319
Let's go with the officers, then.

48
00:03:41,319 --> 00:03:42,360
Okay, I'll go grab something.

49
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:42,680
I'll help you.

50
00:03:48,199 --> 00:03:50,240
Actually, security in Hongye has always been good.

51
00:03:50,639 --> 00:03:51,879
It's one of the best in the province.

52
00:03:52,759 --> 00:03:53,919
Something like today

53
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:55,479
rarely happens even in a decade.

54
00:03:57,039 --> 00:03:59,319
It's my first time running into this.

55
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,599
Now, no matter where I go,

56
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:04,400
I feel Uneasy.

57
00:04:04,919 --> 00:04:05,919
I feel panicky.

58
00:04:07,159 --> 00:04:08,360
I just don't feel safe.

59
00:04:09,439 --> 00:04:10,919
My mentor used to tell me,

60
00:04:11,159 --> 00:04:12,280
in situations like this,

61
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:13,240
the best way

62
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:16,279
is to find a place where you feel safe and secure,

63
00:04:16,519 --> 00:04:17,560
and stay there for a while.

64
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:20,839
Safe?

65
00:04:22,959 --> 00:04:24,839
Where is a safe place in Hongye?

66
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,240
There is.

67
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,439
Right up ahead.

68
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:29,160
Is there anywhere in Hongye

69
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,639
safer than our Special Police Unit?

70
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:32,879
Who would dare cause trouble here?

71
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:48,639
Actually, all of Hongye City is quite safe.

72
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,079
Brother, you haven't left yet?

73
00:06:13,399 --> 00:06:14,560
Job's not done.

74
00:06:15,279 --> 00:06:15,879
Can't leave.

75
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:21,319
So I need a little help from you.

76
00:06:23,279 --> 00:06:24,240
Nothing major.

77
00:06:25,519 --> 00:06:26,959
Just need to stay here for a couple of days.

78
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:29,839
And help us find that woman.

79
00:06:33,319 --> 00:06:34,480
Me, help?

80
00:06:36,759 --> 00:06:38,399
My help got two people next to me killed.

81
00:06:38,399 --> 00:06:40,399
One of them was even a cop.

82
00:06:41,639 --> 00:06:43,519
You two, I really wanted to

83
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,800
do some big things with you.

84
00:06:45,199 --> 00:06:46,279
And learn from you, but

85
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,519
this current situation

86
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,199
is way too big.

87
00:06:51,839 --> 00:06:52,480
Alright.

88
00:06:53,279 --> 00:06:53,800
Help us.

89
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:55,639
Find her.

90
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,240
I guarantee you'll be fine.

91
00:07:10,199 --> 00:07:10,720
The hostage was in danger.

92
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:13,040
We didn't have a clear shot.

93
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,240
Did that shot have to be to the head?

94
00:07:27,839 --> 00:07:28,319
Chief Guo,

95
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:29,879
the Hostage Taker was out of control.

96
00:07:30,199 --> 00:07:31,519
The hostage's life was in danger.

97
00:07:31,879 --> 00:07:33,279
That judgment was made in a split second.

98
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:35,399
Chief Guo,

99
00:07:35,399 --> 00:07:36,560
if I had to do it again, I'd do the same.

100
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:37,360
Do what again?

101
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:38,279
You're really Getting worked up!

102
00:07:38,319 --> 00:07:38,759
What do you mean I'm Getting worked up?

103
00:07:38,759 --> 00:07:39,879
What is a cop supposed to do?

104
00:07:39,879 --> 00:07:40,800
Don't you know?

105
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,000
Are you two fighting in my office?

106
00:07:42,279 --> 00:07:43,199
Take it outside if you want to argue.

107
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:47,680
The people's lives are above all else.

108
00:07:48,279 --> 00:07:50,279
Based on the situation then and the outcome,

109
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:52,160
Liao Bufan's response was not wrong.

110
00:07:54,319 --> 00:07:55,720
Submit a Written Report to me later.

111
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:56,920
Also,

112
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:59,560
Go to the Psychological Intervention Office

113
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:00,399
for an evaluation on time.

114
00:08:00,759 --> 00:08:01,560
Thank you, Chief Guo.

115
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:03,360
I'm mentally stable, no need for an evaluation.

116
00:08:05,319 --> 00:08:06,480
A psychological evaluation

117
00:08:07,439 --> 00:08:08,519
is not based on what you think.

118
00:08:10,199 --> 00:08:11,199
You need to respect science.

119
00:08:15,879 --> 00:08:16,879
Alright, you can go back now.

120
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:18,160
Yes, Chief Guo.

121
00:08:24,399 --> 00:08:24,959
I just don't believe

122
00:08:24,959 --> 00:08:25,920
that if he hadn't fired that shot,

123
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,079
this couldn't have been resolved.

124
00:08:27,079 --> 00:08:28,639
Given the situation, no more hindsight.

125
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:31,079
Can you put the bullet back in the chamber?

126
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:34,240
Now you guys are Getting worked up.

127
00:08:37,559 --> 00:08:38,440
Let's talk about the next case.

128
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:49,559
Jin Yonggang's preliminary autopsy report

129
00:08:49,559 --> 00:08:50,519
has been sent to your computer.

130
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:51,720
You can open it and see.

131
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:56,679
We handed it over to Technical Investigation,

132
00:08:56,679 --> 00:08:59,720
and their frame-by-frame Bodycam analysis

133
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:00,320
is ready.

134
00:09:01,559 --> 00:09:02,720
This previously blurry hand,

135
00:09:02,919 --> 00:09:04,600
after enhancing the resolution for analysis,

136
00:09:04,879 --> 00:09:06,279
shows a mole on the right hand.

137
00:09:06,279 --> 00:09:07,360
But Jin Yonggang doesn't have one on his hand.

138
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,519
So this person isn't Jin Yonggang.

139
00:09:10,559 --> 00:09:11,320
Which means,

140
00:09:11,559 --> 00:09:14,039
one of the two suspects at large

141
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:15,960
must be the one with a right-hand mole.

142
00:09:16,039 --> 00:09:18,759
This is the only physical trait we have right now.

143
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:20,480
Also,

144
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:22,399
inside Jin Yonggang's phone,

145
00:09:22,399 --> 00:09:23,840
we found another SIM card.

146
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:25,120
We didn't know about this before,

147
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,240
because it doesn't belong to him.

148
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:29,320
About an hour before Lu Zhong was killed,

149
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:31,000
an Overseas number

150
00:09:31,519 --> 00:09:34,000
called Jin Yonggang's card.

151
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:37,120
The cell tower is near the Mahjong Parlor.

152
00:09:37,799 --> 00:09:38,600
An Overseas number?

153
00:09:41,159 --> 00:09:42,440
Then do you think it's possible

154
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:44,519
that the killer is from Overseas?

155
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:46,399
Stop with the "is it possible".

156
00:09:47,799 --> 00:09:48,240
Chief Guo,

157
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,000
we will keep investigating,

158
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,639
and report to you when we have concrete news.

159
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:53,120
Understood.

160
00:09:55,399 --> 00:09:57,039
The Task Force must keep this confidential.

161
00:09:57,679 --> 00:09:58,399
Tell the public

162
00:09:58,559 --> 00:09:59,840
that Lu Zhong's case has been solved.

163
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:01,600
From now on,

164
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:04,440
I don't want to hear "is it possible" from you.

165
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:06,360
I want to hear "it is certain."

166
00:10:07,919 --> 00:10:08,440
Yes, sir.

167
00:10:14,519 --> 00:10:14,960
Morning, Director Tan.

168
00:10:15,159 --> 00:10:15,759
Morning, Director Tan.

169
00:10:16,039 --> 00:10:16,440
Morning, Director Tan.

170
00:10:16,879 --> 00:10:17,320
Morning, Director Tan.

171
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:18,080
Morning, Director Tan.

172
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:19,559
You're here, Director Tan.

173
00:10:19,919 --> 00:10:20,679
Morning, Director Zhao.

174
00:10:21,759 --> 00:10:23,600
Director Tan, we heard about yesterday.

175
00:10:23,799 --> 00:10:25,399
Why don't you tell us about it?

176
00:10:26,399 --> 00:10:27,799
Where did these flowers come from?

177
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:32,039
Director Zhao had them placed here.

178
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:34,120
Said it's the icing on the cake for you.

179
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:38,519
Why did I say icing on the cake?

180
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:40,559
Because everyone knows...

181
00:10:41,559 --> 00:10:43,080
that you went into real combat.

182
00:10:43,279 --> 00:10:45,039
And you risked your life for the hostage.

183
00:10:45,559 --> 00:10:47,039
Isn't that just icing on the cake

184
00:10:47,159 --> 00:10:48,240
for our Political Work Department?

185
00:10:51,799 --> 00:10:52,679
The Hostage Taker...

186
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,200
was killed by SWAT.

187
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:57,399
And I didn't even manage to swap the hostage.

188
00:10:57,919 --> 00:10:59,120
I have no merit or credit.

189
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:00,679
It's hardly icing on the cake.

190
00:11:01,159 --> 00:11:03,600
The point isn't whether you swapped the hostage.

191
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:04,840
It's that you dared to go up and try.

192
00:11:05,399 --> 00:11:06,919
I heard it was extremely dangerous yesterday.

193
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,480
Tell everyone about it.

194
00:11:08,519 --> 00:11:10,200
Yeah, Director Tan, tell us about it.

195
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:12,120
Tell us, so we can learn from it.

196
00:11:12,919 --> 00:11:14,919
Of course there was danger.

197
00:11:16,679 --> 00:11:19,440
But when the people are in danger...

198
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:22,200
how could we ignore it?

199
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:27,559
That's very well said.

200
00:11:28,279 --> 00:11:29,720
Whether you're on the Frontline...

201
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:30,960
or in the Political Work Department...

202
00:11:31,679 --> 00:11:32,679
as long as you're a police officer...

203
00:11:32,679 --> 00:11:33,919
you need this Big Picture Perspective.

204
00:11:34,639 --> 00:11:37,799
You have to put the people's lives and property...

205
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:38,879
first.

206
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:41,240
Director Zhao...

207
00:11:41,919 --> 00:11:44,519
a true veteran from the Frontline.

208
00:11:45,679 --> 00:11:48,159
You truly understand public security work.

209
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:49,600
We should all learn from Director Zhao.

210
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:53,679
Director Tan is right.

211
00:11:54,559 --> 00:11:56,360
Stop Sucking up.

212
00:11:56,639 --> 00:11:58,120
How is the banner preparation going?

213
00:11:58,360 --> 00:12:00,360
How is the setup for the Memorial service?

214
00:12:00,559 --> 00:12:01,559
The banner arrived early this morning.

215
00:12:01,759 --> 00:12:03,080
I double-checked it, the wording is fine.

216
00:12:04,759 --> 00:12:07,120
The Calla Lily flowers are all set up too.

217
00:12:09,519 --> 00:12:09,960
Very good.

218
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:10,960
Very good.

219
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:18,679
The hero's deeds...

220
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:20,480
we must heavily promote them.

221
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,279
The hero's flowers must be in the right place.

222
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:27,720
Director Zhao, don't put me on the agenda early.

223
00:12:30,080 --> 00:12:31,360
Let's go check the venue.

224
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:32,279
See how the setup is.

225
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:41,960
That's how he understands it.

226
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:50,000
Put all the flowers on the right, four on the right.

227
00:12:50,799 --> 00:12:51,480
Then over here...

228
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:53,120
Move those two pots in the front to the back.

229
00:12:54,279 --> 00:12:55,639
Be careful on the ladder.

230
00:12:55,639 --> 00:12:56,279
Xiao Qu.

231
00:13:01,159 --> 00:13:01,919
What is it, Director Tan?

232
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:05,399
I think it's lacking something.

233
00:13:05,679 --> 00:13:07,240
That little flowerbed in the middle...

234
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:08,440
How about this...

235
00:13:09,159 --> 00:13:11,519
Look up comrade Lu Zhong's badge number.

236
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,799
Replace the Calla Lily and Chrysanthemum

237
00:13:13,799 --> 00:13:14,799
with his badge number.

238
00:13:19,559 --> 00:13:20,120
Chief Liao.

239
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:22,600
For your Memorial service speech...

240
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:23,840
let's find time to go over it.

241
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:25,159
We have a rehearsal in a couple of days.

242
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:26,399
I'm not giving a speech.

243
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:29,039
That won't do. You and Lu Zhong were partners.

244
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:30,480
Your presence carries weight.

245
00:13:31,679 --> 00:13:34,039
Everyone in the Special Police Unit carries weight.

246
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:34,960
It's different. It's different.

247
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,200
Also, I'm planning to do...

248
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:38,519
an exclusive interview with you.

249
00:13:39,159 --> 00:13:41,960
The title is "Years of training for a single moment."

250
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,639
"SWAT Captain's Single Shot Hits the Mark."

251
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:45,360
Be mentally prepared.

252
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:46,720
Are you done talking?

253
00:13:46,759 --> 00:13:47,200
I'm done.

254
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:49,360
Let's set a time.

255
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:50,159
Set a time.

256
00:13:58,799 --> 00:13:59,279
Come in.

257
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:02,879
Chief Guo.

258
00:14:03,639 --> 00:14:04,519
I have something to discuss.

259
00:14:05,879 --> 00:14:06,279
Come here.

260
00:14:13,799 --> 00:14:15,559
Comrade Lu Zhong's Memorial service speech

261
00:14:15,559 --> 00:14:16,279
is finished.

262
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,559
I'd like you to review it.

263
00:14:20,799 --> 00:14:22,320
Leave professional work to professionals.

264
00:14:22,879 --> 00:14:23,720
With your writing skills,

265
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:25,960
do you really need a former detective like me

266
00:14:26,159 --> 00:14:27,000
to review it?

267
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,039
Absolutely.

268
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:31,799
I'm a bit unsure about the main title.

269
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:32,799
Please take a look.

270
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,159
Oh?

271
00:14:42,519 --> 00:14:43,720
It's written quite well, isn't it?

272
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:46,200
It's quite detailed.

273
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:58,559
"Fervent passion to guard Hongye's happiness;

274
00:14:58,639 --> 00:15:01,519
Utmost loyalty to protect the people's peace."

275
00:15:04,039 --> 00:15:05,559
This is the Fallen hero's Elegiac Couplet.

276
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:08,840
I feel like changing "fervent passion"

277
00:15:09,759 --> 00:15:11,360
to "righteous blood and a loyal heart"

278
00:15:13,759 --> 00:15:14,759
might be slightly better.

279
00:15:15,919 --> 00:15:16,639
Righteous blood and a loyal heart.

280
00:15:18,519 --> 00:15:21,360
"Righteous blood" represents one's devotion

281
00:15:22,159 --> 00:15:23,039
to a just cause.

282
00:15:23,399 --> 00:15:24,440
"Loyal heart" represents

283
00:15:26,039 --> 00:15:27,519
boundless loyalty to the people.

284
00:15:27,519 --> 00:15:28,440
Compared to "fervent passion,"

285
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:30,200
this elevates the message.

286
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:31,799
Have a seat.

287
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:36,080
About the scene yesterday...

288
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:36,879
Chief Guo,

289
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:38,759
I accept the criticism.

290
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:42,559
For us police officers,

291
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:44,480
having courage

292
00:15:44,639 --> 00:15:45,519
is a good thing.

293
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:48,080
But courage alone isn't enough.

294
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:49,759
Take yesterday, for example.

295
00:15:50,639 --> 00:15:52,200
You rushed in recklessly.

296
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:55,279
To yourself, to Ji Min,

297
00:15:55,879 --> 00:15:57,159
and to the hostage's safety,

298
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:59,240
that was extremely irresponsible.

299
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:06,720
I... I was reckless.

300
00:16:07,679 --> 00:16:08,600
Let this be a lesson to you.

301
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:10,159
Yes, sir.

302
00:16:10,919 --> 00:16:11,279
Also,

303
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:14,039
for Comrade Lu Zhong's Memorial service,

304
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,440
put some extra care into it.

305
00:16:16,840 --> 00:16:17,720
Make sure it's flawless,

306
00:16:19,679 --> 00:16:20,799
to give our Fallen hero a proper send-off.

307
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,120
Rest assured,

308
00:16:26,039 --> 00:16:26,679
it will be flawless.

309
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:12,720
After the incident,

310
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:14,400
do you replay the moment you fired?

311
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:15,839
Yes.

312
00:17:17,319 --> 00:17:18,319
Do you think about it often?

313
00:17:19,039 --> 00:17:19,519
No.

314
00:17:21,839 --> 00:17:23,279
I only review it once

315
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:26,519
to make sure my judgment at the time was correct.

316
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,160
Other than the Hostage scene,

317
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:31,200
is there anything else?

318
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:35,680
Yes.

319
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:37,119
What is it?

320
00:17:39,119 --> 00:17:40,240
After the gunshot,

321
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:42,839
I thought of how Commissar Lu looked when he was shot.

322
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:48,839
We were together.

323
00:18:15,279 --> 00:18:15,960
Ma'am

324
00:18:45,519 --> 00:18:46,200
Thank you.

325
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:00,720
The killer has been shot dead.

326
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:39,920
I'm sorry, Ma'am.

327
00:19:43,559 --> 00:19:45,000
I didn't keep Old Lu safe.

328
00:19:45,279 --> 00:19:46,920
If I had been there that day...

329
00:19:47,599 --> 00:19:48,039
No.

330
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:51,480
No one is to blame for this.

331
00:19:56,039 --> 00:19:57,319
This was Old Lu's fate.

332
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:06,119
He chose to be a police officer.

333
00:20:10,279 --> 00:20:11,559
And I chose to marry him.

334
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,640
I just hope...

335
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:21,200
that you all stay safe.

336
00:21:59,160 --> 00:21:59,759
Good morning, Director Tan.

337
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,079
I'm heading to the Union.

338
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:05,119
Director Tan, the Special Police representative is here.

339
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:28,960
The Special Police Unit sent you.

340
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,359
If you're not satisfied,

341
00:22:31,359 --> 00:22:32,559
you can tell Chief Liao directly.

342
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:33,359
Have him send someone else.

343
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:36,759
It's just... it wasn't what I expected.

344
00:22:36,839 --> 00:22:39,480
I thought they'd send someone mature and seasoned.

345
00:22:39,920 --> 00:22:41,039
But they sent someone young.

346
00:22:41,519 --> 00:22:43,519
So I'll have to revise my speech.

347
00:22:45,039 --> 00:22:46,359
Young people may lack experience,

348
00:22:46,559 --> 00:22:47,839
but that doesn't mean they aren't reliable.

349
00:22:49,039 --> 00:22:50,920
With a veteran, the focus must be

350
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,160
on shared hardships and reminiscing.

351
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:56,720
With youth, there's vitality,

352
00:22:57,680 --> 00:23:00,759
so it must be about carrying the torch forward.

353
00:23:04,640 --> 00:23:06,720
Director Tan, you don't need to tell me all this.

354
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:09,000
You can revise the speech however you want.

355
00:23:09,279 --> 00:23:10,000
I'll just read from it.

356
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:11,480
As long as I complete the mission.

357
00:23:14,079 --> 00:23:15,160
Comrade Bai Jiani,

358
00:23:17,079 --> 00:23:19,400
you coming... coming here

359
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:21,559
isn't just about completing a mission

360
00:23:21,759 --> 00:23:22,720
or going through the motions.

361
00:23:23,480 --> 00:23:25,319
Comrade Lu Zhong's Memorial service

362
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:27,880
isn't just a platform to praise

363
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:29,000
his personal heroic deeds,

364
00:23:29,319 --> 00:23:30,279
it's also a powerful expression

365
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:32,519
of the Hongye Police Spirit

366
00:23:32,519 --> 00:23:34,240
and the Public Security Spirit.

367
00:23:35,359 --> 00:23:36,720
When you give your speech,

368
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:38,920
if you don't take it seriously,

369
00:23:39,319 --> 00:23:41,000
you're not taking Commissar Lu seriously.

370
00:23:41,599 --> 00:23:43,640
And worse, you're disrespecting the Hongye Police Spirit

371
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:46,079
and the Public Security Spirit.

372
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:49,440
Do you think that's appropriate?

373
00:23:50,920 --> 00:23:52,599
If you think it is,

374
00:23:53,799 --> 00:23:55,079
then why would I insist on

375
00:23:55,079 --> 00:23:56,119
having the Special Police Unit here?

376
00:23:57,400 --> 00:23:59,759
I asked them to send a representative for one reason:

377
00:24:01,359 --> 00:24:03,000
genuine sincerity.

378
00:24:09,319 --> 00:24:09,640
Fine.

379
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:53,400
Director Tan.

380
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:55,960
Deputy Director Tan.

381
00:24:56,599 --> 00:24:58,359
The leaders are all here today, so watch what you say.

382
00:24:58,559 --> 00:24:59,960
It's just a matter of time, isn't it?

383
00:25:00,079 --> 00:25:01,039
Thought I'd start using it early.

384
00:25:01,319 --> 00:25:01,839
What is it?

385
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:03,839
The speakers and mics are all set.

386
00:25:04,039 --> 00:25:05,880
Double-check them to ensure nothing goes wrong.

387
00:25:06,160 --> 00:25:06,400
Alright!

388
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:07,559
What's that on your mouth? Wipe it off.

389
00:25:47,279 --> 00:25:47,880
Relax.

390
00:26:10,960 --> 00:26:12,599
Distinguished leaders, comrades,

391
00:26:13,279 --> 00:26:15,759
I am Bai Jiani, spokesperson for the Special Police Unit.

392
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:17,839
Today,

393
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:19,880
with heavy hearts,

394
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:23,880
we gather here to remember our good comrade, a fine police officer,

395
00:26:24,799 --> 00:26:27,240
former Political Commissar of the Hongye City Public Security Bureau's Special Police Unit,

396
00:26:27,799 --> 00:26:28,720
Comrade Lu Zhong.

397
00:26:43,359 --> 00:26:45,240
Commissar Lu brought me in via Civilian Recruitment.

398
00:26:47,720 --> 00:26:48,640
Before that,

399
00:26:49,319 --> 00:26:50,559
I had no goal in life.

400
00:26:51,359 --> 00:26:53,000
But after joining the Special Police Unit,

401
00:26:53,359 --> 00:26:54,960
I think I found my direction.

402
00:26:55,920 --> 00:26:57,400
I wanted to be a good special police officer,

403
00:26:57,839 --> 00:26:59,720
to become an excellent Sniper.

404
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:01,440
I owe it all to Commissar Lu.

405
00:27:02,319 --> 00:27:04,000
Commissar Lu was a very optimistic person.

406
00:27:04,720 --> 00:27:06,359
No matter how hard, tiring,

407
00:27:06,640 --> 00:27:07,559
or dangerous the job was,

408
00:27:07,839 --> 00:27:09,039
he was always cheerful.

409
00:27:10,079 --> 00:27:10,920
In my three years on the team,

410
00:27:11,640 --> 00:27:13,079
the things I saw him worry about most

411
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:14,839
were broken training equipment

412
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:16,400
and how to request replacements.

413
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:18,480
When funds were short,

414
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:20,000
he would pay out of his own pocket.

415
00:27:21,039 --> 00:27:22,400
And he was the one running around

416
00:27:22,839 --> 00:27:24,400
to secure training grounds for us.

417
00:27:25,720 --> 00:27:26,799
Every time Commissar Lu talked

418
00:27:26,799 --> 00:27:28,119
about our Special Police Unit,

419
00:27:28,640 --> 00:27:29,640
he was always so proud,

420
00:27:31,200 --> 00:27:32,440
because we had the best gear,

421
00:27:32,759 --> 00:27:33,680
the best physical fitness,

422
00:27:33,720 --> 00:27:35,279
and were the most accurate shooters.

423
00:27:35,920 --> 00:27:37,039
But he still couldn't understand

424
00:27:37,759 --> 00:27:39,160
why our Special Police Unit

425
00:27:39,680 --> 00:27:40,720
could never retain its people.

426
00:28:00,559 --> 00:28:01,480
Thank you, leaders.

427
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:02,720
That concludes my speech.

428
00:28:20,079 --> 00:28:20,519
I'll go.

429
00:28:37,319 --> 00:28:37,680
Hello everyone.

430
00:28:38,480 --> 00:28:39,880
I am the Publicity Department's

431
00:28:41,119 --> 00:28:42,200
spokesperson, Tan Yan.

432
00:28:43,960 --> 00:28:45,559
At such events, people are used to

433
00:28:45,559 --> 00:28:47,079
only talking about loyalty and faith.

434
00:28:48,160 --> 00:28:51,160
Officer Lu Zhong already possessed such qualities.

435
00:28:53,839 --> 00:28:54,359
I think

436
00:28:55,559 --> 00:28:56,519
we should focus more on

437
00:28:57,079 --> 00:28:58,720
the true burdens

438
00:28:59,920 --> 00:29:01,160
carried in a hero's heart,

439
00:29:02,160 --> 00:29:03,359
and the responsibilities they bear.

440
00:29:04,640 --> 00:29:05,119
Distinguished leaders,

441
00:29:06,599 --> 00:29:07,039
fellow officers.

442
00:29:08,920 --> 00:29:10,119
At this hero's Memorial service,

443
00:29:11,200 --> 00:29:14,640
we don't want to use grand words and cliches anymore.

444
00:29:15,440 --> 00:29:18,319
We just want everyone to truly understand

445
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:20,759
the hardships of Frontline Police Officers.

446
00:29:23,640 --> 00:29:24,400
We all know

447
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:26,279
what it means to be a police officer.

448
00:29:27,799 --> 00:29:29,680
It means rushing to the Frontline,

449
00:29:31,039 --> 00:29:33,680
facing the most dangerous criminals,

450
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:37,039
and enduring countless sleepless nights.

451
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:38,240
It also means

452
00:29:38,359 --> 00:29:40,160
that any of us could be the next

453
00:29:40,440 --> 00:29:40,880
Lu Zhong.

454
00:29:42,839 --> 00:29:43,519
As police officers,

455
00:29:43,519 --> 00:29:45,480
we've always been prepared to sacrifice.

456
00:29:46,960 --> 00:29:48,119
But our families

457
00:29:49,319 --> 00:29:51,039
keep waking up in the middle of the night,

458
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:54,559
terrified that a single phone call

459
00:29:57,079 --> 00:29:58,720
will take away their loved ones.

460
00:30:01,559 --> 00:30:02,039
I think,

461
00:30:03,480 --> 00:30:04,839
aside from being police officers,

462
00:30:06,319 --> 00:30:07,680
we are also fathers to our children,

463
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,759
husbands to our wives,

464
00:30:10,359 --> 00:30:11,440
and children to our parents.

465
00:30:13,319 --> 00:30:14,480
Shouldn't we

466
00:30:14,799 --> 00:30:16,160
do something for them?

467
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:18,599
Shouldn't we think about

468
00:30:19,119 --> 00:30:20,799
how to ensure that every officer,

469
00:30:21,240 --> 00:30:23,119
while devoting to the mission,

470
00:30:23,839 --> 00:30:25,920
can also receive better support?

471
00:30:45,319 --> 00:30:47,440
Sacrifice shouldn't just be remembered.

472
00:30:49,039 --> 00:30:50,279
It should serve as our

473
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:52,759
driving force for change.

474
00:30:56,079 --> 00:30:57,160
The fewer Memorial services like this,

475
00:30:58,680 --> 00:30:59,640
the better.

476
00:31:37,160 --> 00:31:38,960
If you have any difficulties, please let us know.

477
00:31:38,960 --> 00:31:39,920
Thank you, sir.

478
00:31:41,079 --> 00:31:41,759
My deepest condolences.

479
00:31:41,759 --> 00:31:42,519
Thank you, sir.

480
00:31:55,720 --> 00:31:56,759
Thank you, Director Tan.

481
00:32:39,079 --> 00:32:40,759
Not bad, Tan.

482
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:43,200
Very touching.

483
00:32:45,200 --> 00:32:47,000
Nobody does it like you, Tan.

484
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:42,200
Did Chief Guo transfer you back?

485
00:33:42,960 --> 00:33:43,440
No.

486
00:33:44,440 --> 00:33:45,440
I applied to come back myself.

487
00:33:49,799 --> 00:33:51,599
You went through all that trouble

488
00:33:52,039 --> 00:33:53,559
to finally get into the Traffic Police,

489
00:33:54,480 --> 00:33:55,680
so why bother coming back now?

490
00:33:59,160 --> 00:33:59,920
Because of Old Lu?

491
00:34:02,079 --> 00:34:02,720
Not entirely.

492
00:34:03,519 --> 00:34:04,319
Mainly because in the Traffic Police,

493
00:34:04,319 --> 00:34:05,640
I'd seriously had enough of it.

494
00:34:05,640 --> 00:34:06,279
Let me tell you,

495
00:34:06,720 --> 00:34:07,799
I've wanted to come back to the team for ages.

496
00:34:08,159 --> 00:34:09,400
I just couldn't get a chance.

497
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:10,920
You know?

498
00:34:12,639 --> 00:34:14,000
Brother Lang, what about

499
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:14,800
Ma'am?

500
00:34:14,800 --> 00:34:15,960
My wife fully supports me.

501
00:34:16,199 --> 00:34:17,239
She respects my wishes.

502
00:34:17,239 --> 00:34:18,000
Don't worry about that.

503
00:34:20,760 --> 00:34:22,239
Alright, since you're back,

504
00:34:22,239 --> 00:34:23,719
what's with all the talk? Get in there.

505
00:34:25,360 --> 00:34:26,000
Where are the guys?

506
00:34:26,400 --> 00:34:27,320
They're in our gym.

507
00:35:07,320 --> 00:35:08,039
You're home.

508
00:35:09,639 --> 00:35:10,760
No overtime today?

509
00:35:11,559 --> 00:35:12,039
I am.

510
00:35:12,480 --> 00:35:14,000
I came back to grab some clean clothes.

511
00:35:18,119 --> 00:35:19,239
A Deputy Chief

512
00:35:19,960 --> 00:35:21,000
busier than the Chief himself.

513
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:26,960
Have you eaten?

514
00:35:28,079 --> 00:35:28,480
I have.

515
00:35:29,440 --> 00:35:30,159
I haven't eaten yet.

516
00:35:40,599 --> 00:35:42,440
You don't want dumplings, wontons,

517
00:35:43,840 --> 00:35:44,920
steamed buns, or rolls.

518
00:35:45,559 --> 00:35:46,559
I don't feel like eating either.

519
00:35:50,079 --> 00:35:51,639
Just have some Soda water then.

520
00:35:57,199 --> 00:35:57,920
What are you writing?

521
00:35:57,920 --> 00:35:58,800
Do you need help?

522
00:35:59,719 --> 00:36:00,159
No need.

523
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:01,679
Almost done.

524
00:36:03,039 --> 00:36:05,400
I'm applying for a Community Subsidy for Mr. Jin.

525
00:36:08,039 --> 00:36:10,320
Did you hear about the Memorial service today?

526
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:13,719
I did.

527
00:36:16,159 --> 00:36:17,760
I wonder what the consequences will be.

528
00:36:18,320 --> 00:36:20,119
What consequences can there be for telling the truth?

529
00:36:22,360 --> 00:36:23,880
Our comrade died.

530
00:36:24,880 --> 00:36:26,119
My original intention was

531
00:36:26,119 --> 00:36:28,320
to spread the hero's spirit further.

532
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:31,199
I didn't expect this...

533
00:36:33,480 --> 00:36:34,400
Actually, today,

534
00:36:34,760 --> 00:36:36,000
I felt quite emotional too.

535
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:37,239
The few of us

536
00:36:37,599 --> 00:36:39,400
graduated from the Police Academy together.

537
00:36:40,440 --> 00:36:41,599
Take Old Zhang, he's already

538
00:36:42,159 --> 00:36:43,880
the Captain of Narcotics Control.

539
00:36:44,559 --> 00:36:46,840
Old Na is the head of Criminal Investigation.

540
00:36:47,519 --> 00:36:50,960
Lin Nan excels in the Economic Crime Investigation Unit.

541
00:36:52,440 --> 00:36:53,320
And you, Deputy Chief Ji,

542
00:36:53,320 --> 00:36:56,079
at least have dozens of people under you.

543
00:36:57,519 --> 00:37:00,719
I've been stuck in the Publicity Department all these years,

544
00:37:03,039 --> 00:37:04,800
and I'm still just a Deputy Director.

545
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:09,280
I finally made it to

546
00:37:10,119 --> 00:37:11,159
Director Gu's retirement.

547
00:37:11,159 --> 00:37:12,360
Of course I want

548
00:37:13,280 --> 00:37:14,159
to move up as soon as possible.

549
00:37:14,320 --> 00:37:15,239
Am I wrong for that?

550
00:37:19,440 --> 00:37:20,960
So you can safely step down from the Frontline.

551
00:37:22,159 --> 00:37:22,840
Is there a problem

552
00:37:23,719 --> 00:37:24,440
with my plan?

553
00:37:24,880 --> 00:37:25,760
How does your promotion to Director

554
00:37:26,320 --> 00:37:27,880
conflict with me being on the Frontline?

555
00:37:28,039 --> 00:37:28,920
The Frontline is dangerous.

556
00:37:32,960 --> 00:37:33,960
You can't avoid what's coming.

557
00:37:34,679 --> 00:37:35,599
It doesn't matter where you are.

558
00:37:36,039 --> 00:37:38,960
Anyway, you can't stay at the Police Station forever.

559
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:42,719
I've got it all planned out for you.

560
00:37:44,920 --> 00:37:47,079
Right, but things don't always go as planned.

561
00:37:52,239 --> 00:37:54,039
Do you know what the problem between us is?

562
00:37:56,480 --> 00:37:57,119
What problem?

563
00:38:00,599 --> 00:38:01,320
Do we have a problem?

564
00:38:06,599 --> 00:38:07,559
Then... then tell me.

565
00:38:08,440 --> 00:38:09,360
What problem do we have?

566
00:38:21,280 --> 00:38:22,280
Our biggest problem

567
00:38:23,599 --> 00:38:24,159
is that

568
00:38:24,920 --> 00:38:26,599
you think everything's fine.

569
00:38:28,320 --> 00:38:29,360
I've always thought everything was fine.

570
00:38:37,079 --> 00:38:38,559
Old Guo asked me to go fishing.

571
00:38:44,199 --> 00:38:44,880
I'll take a cab.

572
00:38:47,280 --> 00:38:48,159
I need to change.

573
00:38:48,719 --> 00:38:49,320
Where are my clothes?

574
00:39:02,679 --> 00:39:03,119
Old Lyu!

575
00:39:04,559 --> 00:39:05,719
You gotta bring the food out faster.

576
00:39:06,159 --> 00:39:07,079
Can't go any faster.

577
00:39:07,079 --> 00:39:08,320
You shouldn't have even come back.

578
00:39:08,559 --> 00:39:09,960
Do you know what time it is? Still Bothering me.

579
00:39:10,360 --> 00:39:11,920
It's not like I'm Bothering you every day.

580
00:39:13,480 --> 00:39:16,039
Brother Lang, when are you leaving this time?

581
00:39:16,840 --> 00:39:17,639
Yeah, Brother Lang.

582
00:39:17,800 --> 00:39:18,599
When are you leaving?

583
00:39:22,440 --> 00:39:22,840
Alright, alright, alright.

584
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:23,719
Everyone, keep it down.

585
00:39:24,119 --> 00:39:24,639
Listen to me.

586
00:39:27,880 --> 00:39:29,559
Before, I was on secondment.

587
00:39:30,519 --> 00:39:32,119
What's borrowed must be returned.

588
00:39:32,920 --> 00:39:33,599
Understood?

589
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:35,679
This time I'm back,

590
00:39:36,880 --> 00:39:37,639
and I'm not leaving!

591
00:39:38,280 --> 00:39:39,360
Because this is my home.

592
00:39:40,840 --> 00:39:41,519
Got it?

593
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:43,039
Did Ma'am agree to this?

594
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:44,800
Are you serious?

595
00:39:45,360 --> 00:39:47,440
You'll be In the doghouse back home.

596
00:39:51,679 --> 00:39:52,559
Let me say a few words.

597
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:53,960
Since the food isn't here yet anyway.

598
00:39:56,719 --> 00:39:58,239
Today is a special day.

599
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:05,039
We bid Commissar Lu a final farewell.

600
00:40:06,880 --> 00:40:07,960
We also welcome our Brother Lang,

601
00:40:09,079 --> 00:40:10,239
Captain Liu, back home.

602
00:40:15,360 --> 00:40:17,239
Commissar Lu once told me something.

603
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:24,039
The departed have passed on;

604
00:40:28,519 --> 00:40:29,599
the living must carry on.

605
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:34,800
I'm a simple guy.

606
00:40:35,400 --> 00:40:36,599
I didn't get what it meant.

607
00:40:36,679 --> 00:40:37,719
But I thought about it,

608
00:40:40,039 --> 00:40:40,920
and I think it means

609
00:40:41,360 --> 00:40:42,320
the living

610
00:40:44,199 --> 00:40:44,880
should live well.

611
00:40:48,280 --> 00:40:50,400
Let the past be the past.

612
00:40:53,679 --> 00:40:54,119
But,

613
00:40:55,320 --> 00:40:55,920
the past

614
00:40:58,480 --> 00:40:59,480
doesn't mean forgetting.

615
00:41:02,280 --> 00:41:03,639
So, we who are still alive

616
00:41:05,119 --> 00:41:06,480
must do right by those who have passed.

617
00:41:12,599 --> 00:41:13,239
How do we do that?

618
00:41:20,880 --> 00:41:21,760
In this year's Combat Skills Competition,

619
00:41:26,480 --> 00:41:27,360
are you all confident?

620
00:41:28,400 --> 00:41:29,320
Yes!

621
00:41:31,360 --> 00:41:32,719
We have to be confident.

622
00:41:35,679 --> 00:41:37,119
Why wouldn't we be?

623
00:41:39,119 --> 00:41:39,599
In our team,

624
00:41:41,199 --> 00:41:43,000
every single one is a top-tier expert.

625
00:41:44,239 --> 00:41:45,880
For shooting, we have Bai Jiani.

626
00:41:46,280 --> 00:41:46,920
For sparring,

627
00:41:47,239 --> 00:41:48,039
we have Wang Yunsheng.

628
00:41:49,400 --> 00:41:49,840
Yunsheng,

629
00:41:51,039 --> 00:41:51,840
what we talked about before,

630
00:41:52,119 --> 00:41:52,679
the physical training,

631
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:53,599
you haven't stopped, right?

632
00:41:54,519 --> 00:41:55,199
He hasn't stopped.

633
00:41:55,800 --> 00:41:56,599
Every day after morning practice,

634
00:41:56,880 --> 00:41:57,679
he runs with us.

635
00:41:57,800 --> 00:41:58,159
Good!

636
00:41:59,920 --> 00:42:01,239
The time to earn merit for the team has come.

637
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:03,960
Come on, come on.

638
00:42:04,599 --> 00:42:06,079
Let's start with a couple of dishes first.

639
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:12,280
This is the Small bottle of liquor Commissar Lu saved.

640
00:42:13,519 --> 00:42:14,920
Why didn't Commissar Lu come today?

641
00:42:32,840 --> 00:42:34,039
Let's keep saving this bottle.

642
00:42:35,760 --> 00:42:37,519
Right, save it for now.

643
00:42:38,960 --> 00:42:40,440
Once we place in the Combat Skills Competition,

644
00:42:40,679 --> 00:42:41,119
we'll drink it then.

645
00:42:44,400 --> 00:42:45,440
Just placing isn't enough.

646
00:42:47,239 --> 00:42:48,039
We need to get first place.

647
00:42:52,280 --> 00:42:53,239
Commissar Lu said,

648
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:55,719
first place stands highest.

649
00:43:12,119 --> 00:43:13,519
From Bai Jiani,

650
00:43:13,519 --> 00:43:15,679
you can see our Special Police Unit's

651
00:43:15,920 --> 00:43:17,639
shortcomings and weaknesses.

652
00:43:17,840 --> 00:43:19,880
It has been decided that Comrade Tan Yan

653
00:43:19,880 --> 00:43:21,960
will do a secondment as Special Police Unit Commissar.

654
00:43:22,079 --> 00:43:23,320
So you're taking a guy

655
00:43:23,400 --> 00:43:24,880
who only knows how to write reports

656
00:43:24,880 --> 00:43:26,079
and dumping him on our Special Police Unit?

657
00:43:26,079 --> 00:43:26,920
I refuse to accept this.

658
00:43:26,960 --> 00:43:28,840
We really can't blame anyone else.

659
00:43:28,840 --> 00:43:30,639
We just can't retain people here ourselves.

660
00:43:30,960 --> 00:43:31,599
I just hope that you

661
00:43:31,599 --> 00:43:33,360
can solve all those problems for me.

662
00:43:33,800 --> 00:43:34,239
No way.

663
00:43:34,480 --> 00:43:36,000
I have to put him in his place.
